# Cross-Platform Integration Standards

## Shared Architecture
### Code Organization
```typescript
src/
  shared/           // Shared business logic
    types/
    utils/
    hooks/
  platform/         // Platform-specific code
    mobile/
    web/
    server/
```

## Component Design
### Shared Components
```typescript
// Example shared component
interface ButtonProps {
  label: string;
  onPress: () => void;
  variant: 'primary' | 'secondary';
}

// Platform-specific implementations
const Button = Platform.select({
  ios: IOSButton,
  web: WebButton,
  default: DefaultButton,
});
```

## State Management
- Consistent state architecture
- Platform-agnostic business logic
- Unified data flow patterns
- Shared type definitions

## Asset Management
### Organization
```
assets/
  shared/
    icons/
    images/
  platform/
    ios/
    web/
```

### Implementation
- Platform-specific optimizations
- Shared asset naming conventions
- Responsive asset loading
- Efficient caching strategies

## Testing Strategy
### Shared Tests
- Business logic unit tests
- Shared component tests
- Type checking
- Integration tests

### Platform Tests
- Platform-specific UI tests
- Performance benchmarks
- Device compatibility
- Network handling

## Development Workflow
### Environment Setup
- Unified development scripts
- Shared configuration
- Common tooling (ESLint, Prettier)
- Consistent versioning

### Deployment
- Platform-specific builds
- Shared CI/CD pipelines
- Environment management
- Release coordination